  ('cos-201-java-programming', 'COS 201: Computer Programming I (Java)', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Agriculture', 'Computer Science', '200 Level', 'Which keyword is used to declare that a method may throw a particular checked exception, without handling it inside the method itself?', '["Throw", "Throws", "Catch", "Except"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Throws (with an ''s'') appears in a method''s header/signature to declare that calling this method might result in the named exception propagating out of it, e.g. `public void readFile throws IOException {.. }`.', 'Keywords', false, 'first', 2),
  ('cos-201-java-programming', 'COS 201: Computer Programming I (Java)', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Agriculture', 'Computer Science', '200 Level', 'Which keyword is used to test an assertion (a condition expected to always be true) during development, typically disabled by default at runtime?', '["Assert", "Verify", "Check", "Test"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Assert is Java''s keyword for writing assertions -- runtime checks of conditions expected to always hold, primarily used during development/testing and typically disabled by default in production unless explicitly enabled.', 'Keywords', false, 'first', 2),
  ('cos-201-java-programming', 'COS 201: Computer Programming I (Java)', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Agriculture', 'Computer Science', '200 Level', 'What is the value of `x` after this code runs?
