  ('cos-201-java-programming', 'COS 201: Computer Programming I (Java)', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Agriculture', 'Computer Science', '200 Level', 'What is the value type and content of `char letter = ''x''; int code = letter;`?', '["A compile-time error, since char cannot be assigned to int", "Code holds the integer Unicode/ASCII value of ''x'' (120), because char widens automatically to int", "Code holds the String \"x\"", "Code holds 0"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Char is an unsigned 16-bit type that widens automatically (without an explicit cast) into int, taking on the character''s underlying numeric code -- ''x'' has Unicode/ASCII value 120, so code becomes 120.', 'Data Types', false, 'first', 2),
  ('cos-201-java-programming', 'COS 201: Computer Programming I (Java)', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Agriculture', 'Computer Science', '200 Level', 'Which of the following correctly declares an array of 5 integers in Java?', '["Int numbers[5];", "Int[] numbers = new int[5];", "Array numbers = int[5];", "Int numbers = new array(5);"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The standard Java syntax for creating a fixed-size array of 5 ints is `int[] numbers = new int[5];` (declaring the array type with new and a size).', 'Data Types', false, 'first', 2),
  ('cos-201-java-programming', 'COS 201: Computer Programming I (Java)', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Agriculture', 'Computer Science', '200 Level', 'In the Account class example, what would `public Account(String initialName) { name = initialName; }` added to the class allow a caller to do?', '["Nothing different from before; constructors have no effect on object creation", "Create an Account object with its name already set in the same statement, e.g. `Account a = new Account(\"Ada\");`, instead of needing a separate setName call afterward", "Delete the setName method automatically", "Force every Account to have the same name"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Adding this constructor lets a caller supply the initial name directly as an argument to new, e.g. `new Account("Ada")`, setting the name in one step rather than needing to call setName separately afterward.', 'Classes, Objects and Methods', false, 'first', 2),
  ('cos-201-java-programming', 'COS 201: Computer Programming I (Java)', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Agriculture', 'Computer Science', '200 Level', 'What is the output of the following code?
int a = 8;
int b = 3;
System.out.println(a % b + " " + a / b);', '["2 2", "2 2.67", "2 3", "8 3"]'::jsonb, 0, '8 % 3 leaves remainder 2 (since 3*2=6, 8-6=2). 8 / 3 with two int operands performs integer division, giving 2 (discarding the fractional part). Concatenated with a space between: "2 2".', 'Operators', false, 'first', 2),
  ('cos-201-java-programming', 'COS 201: Computer Programming I (Java)', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Agriculture', 'Computer Science', '200 Level', 'What is the output of the following code?
String s = "Java";
System.out.println(s.length);', '["3", "4", "5", "A compile-time error"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The String "Java" contains 4 characters (J, a, v, a), so calling length on it returns 4.', 'Data Types', false, 'first', 2);
